WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
SPEAKER: If you
are an enterprise,

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.950
chances are you have
networking, storage, and compute

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.800
on multiple clouds and
in your own data center.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.640
How can you consistently secure
and operate existing apps,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.800
develop and deploy
the new apps across

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.690
those disparate locations?

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.510
How can you get centralized
visibility and management

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.950
of those resources?

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.026
Well, that is why Anthos exists.

00:00:23.026 --> 00:00:26.994
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.990
Welcome to Anthos 101.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.970
As an enterprise,
it is very common

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.320
to have an existing
networking, storage,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.760
and compute on multiple clouds
and in your own data centers.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.030
On each of these platforms you
need to manage infrastructure.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.160
Let's say you use
containers on the clouds

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:49.150
and develop apps using services
on Google Cloud and AWS.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.420
Regardless of platform, you
will need policy enforcement

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.520
across your IT footprint.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.590
To manage these
across platforms,

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.140
you need monitoring
and logging systems,

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.150
and you need to
integrate that data

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.790
into meaningful categories,
like business data,

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.070
operational data, and alerts.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.460
Digging further, you might use
operational data and alerts

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.220
to inform optimizations,
automations,

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.800
and to set policies or SLOs.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:17.800
You might use business
data to do all those things

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.290
and to deploy third-party apps.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.980
Then, to actually enact the
changes you've decided on,

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:27.590
you need to act on different
specific parts of the system.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:31.090
That means digging into each
tool for policy enforcement,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.900
securing services, orchestrating
containers, and managing

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.940
infrastructure management.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.280
Oh, and don't forget,
all of this work

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:42.970
is in addition to what it
takes to develop and deploy

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:44.810
your own apps.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.620
Now, consider repeating
this set of tasks and data

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.800
across a hybrid and
multi-cloud landscape.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.800
It becomes very, very
complex very quickly.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.350
Your platform
admins, SREs, DevOps

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.720
who are responsible for
security and efficiency

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.140
have manual cluster by cluster
management, data collection,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.030
and information synthesis.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.670
With this complexity,
it's hard to stay current,

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.500
to understand
business implications,

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.590
and to ensure compliance,
not to mention the difficulty

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.580
onboarding a new hire.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.240
Anthos helps solve
these challenges.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.250
With Anthos, you
get a consistent way

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.070
to manage with similar
infrastructure management,

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.520
container management, service
management, and policy

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.190
enforcement across
your platform.

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.830
As a result, you
gain observability

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:33.050
across your platforms
in one single place,

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.620
including business
information, alerts,

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.930
and operational information.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.470
With this information, you might
decide to optimize, automate,

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.290
and set policies
or SLOs, or might

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.180
rely on our machine
learning models

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.490
to make automated suggestions.

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:51.970
You take those recommendations
or make your own decisions

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.090
and apply them to different
management layers.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.530
Simple, right?

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.190
Not quite.

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:00.970
You may have different regions
that need different policies

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.520
and also have different
development, staging,

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.700
or production environments that
need different permissions.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.820
Some parts of your work
may need more security.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.830
That's where environs come in.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.590
Environs are the way
to create logical sets

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.750
of underlying
Kubernetes clusters,

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.870
regardless of which platform
these clusters live on.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.480
By considering grouping
and managing sets

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.060
of clusters as
logical environs, you

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.640
can think about and work
with your applications

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.860
at the right level of detail
for what you need to do,

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:33.700
be it business insights
over the entire system,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.340
setting for a dev environment,
or troubleshooting

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:38.740
data for a specific cluster.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.590
Using environs, each part
of the functional stack

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:44.710
can take declarative
direction about configuration,

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.870
compliance, and more.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:50.440
Anthos provides platform
administrators a single place

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:54.250
to monitor and manage their
landscape, including policy

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.800
control and marketplace access.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.220
This reduces person hours
in management, enforcement,

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.490
discovery, and communication.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.800
Anthos also provides them an
out-of-the-box structured view

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:09.120
of their entire system,
including services, clusters,

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.610
and more, simplifying their
view and management so they can

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.970
improve security, use
resources more efficiently,

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.260
and demonstrate
measurable success.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.500
Anthos is also a
platform to modernize

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.880
application development.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:22.570
Why?

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.110
Because it uses environs to
enforce policies and processes

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.870
and abstracts away that cluster
and container management

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.610
from the application teams.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.160
Anthos allows you to
easily abstract away

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.320
infrastructure from
application teams

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.080
by making it easy for
them to incorporate

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:42.100
a wide variety of CICD
solutions on top of environs,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.740
allowing you to view and
manage your applications

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.610
at the right level of detail.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.180
Here are the key components
of Anthos delivering

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.220
the capabilities we discussed.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:54.070
Anthos simplifies and
provides a consistent view

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:56.170
across your company's
landscape so you

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.790
can improve security, use
resources more efficiently,

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:03.730
innovate faster, and
demonstrate measurable success.

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:06.460
Now, that's a pretty
high-level overview of Anthos.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.110
In the next video,
we will show you

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.990
how to get started with
Anthos on Google Cloud.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.050
Until then, like, subscribe,
and follow the links below

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.540
to learn more about Anthos.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:20.190
